The robot can be classified as a hybrid model which combines the deliberative aspects of feedback control with the reactivity of feedforward control.
The feedback control is clearly sensing, thinking then acting, while the feedforward control maps the desired velocities directly to the controller output.
There's not really any subsumption going on with just the control, with the sole directive of the robot being following the trajectory, though joint limit constraints and such can override the controller, so if one wants to count that then sure.
There's also no layering in terms of e.g. kinematic controller -> dynamic controller or feedback linearization (from what can be seen in joint_controller).
